65c13bc75d508d3d849520fb	Bethesda Thrift Shop	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707162704655.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Exterior_Riley.JPG" width="503" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163031221.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Books_Riley.JPG" width="504" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707162992366.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_ChildrensToysGames_Riley_001.JPG" width="501" style="aspect-ratio: 0.666667 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163114013.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_ChildrensToysGames_Riley_002.JPG" width="499" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163178439.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Clothing_Riley.JPG" width="498" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163215580.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Cross_Riley.JPG" width="496" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163265951.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_FramesFaith_Riley.JPG" width="495" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163308397.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Holiday_Riley.JPG" width="494" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163348439.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Sign_Riley.JPG" width="492" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707163385767.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190714_BethesdaThriftShop_Interior_Vintage_Riley.JPG" width="491" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">While the chaotic Manchester Avenue in Ballwin buzzes with rush hour traffic, a little shop in a strip mall right next to it feels like a welcoming home. Upon walking in, a little bell above the door dings and the friendly cashier greets everyone by name and asks about their family. This warm environment only continues throughout the store. The room is mostly quiet for a calm shopping atmosphere, but customers can still hear the sounds of the hangers scratching on the metal clothing racks as people look through the clothes and the sound of the 90s and early 2000s top hits playing on the speakers -- which the cashier sings along too. The customers are almost all elderly people looking for deals and most of them seem to be regulars, who chat with the workers about life updates. Since the thrift store has a Lutheran mission behind it, there are many decorative crosses, home decor with the word “faith” in it, and a lot of books and movies about Jesus. However, while there is a religious purpose that drives the store, it isn’t too overt for the customers. The only religious values that are completely obvious to Bethesda’s visitors are the kindness and welcoming nature that the store offers for its customers.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Are the visitors of Bethesda Thrift Shop mostly coming for the store itself or do they like to support its Lutheran roots?<br></span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Do the workers all follow the Lutheran denomination?</span><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">What does a typical day look like for Bethesda with its number and typical demographic of customers?</span></p><p></p><p></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The loudest noises in the store that you notice as soon as you walk in is the music playing over the speakers and the sound of metal hangers scrapping the metal clothing racks while people look through the clothes</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The music in the speakers is all 90’s and early 2000’s hits</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A woman standing at the cash register in the middle of the store said hi and welcomed me to the store</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are a few groups around the store looking through the objects already</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Every time a new person walks into the store, a bell above the door rings and the cashier greets them, she knows every person that has walked in so far and has greeted them by name</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">One worker in the back of the store is sorting through glassware, the sound of glass clinking together becomes louder every time she comes out from the back room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There seems to be four workers in the store -- three middle-aged females and one older male</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The male worker is putting up a new flag outside the store while the female workers are at the register or sorting through products inside</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Almost all of the customers are older, there’s only one middle-aged mom with her two young girls in the store that differ from that</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Right when you walk in, you see the cashier at the counter in the middle of the room. On the left of that is the women’s clothing section and on the right is the men’s clothing section. Behind all of that are the kitchenware, glass, books, movies, furniture, toys, and pet section</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are four plaques on the wall scattered around the store that say the store’s mission and their background story</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">From the plaques I learned that it is a Lutheran thrift store</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There is one man that walks in that grabs a cart and immediately begins filling it with old electronics, the cashier knows him by name and he seems to be a regular there</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The woman at the register sings along loudly to the songs on the speaker. She seems to be very happy to work there</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Another worker walks over to the register and talks with the cashier, they seem to be friends because they kindly ask about each other’s lives</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">As each person comes to check out, the cashier begins to have a lengthy conversation with them, asking them lots of questions about their day and what their plans are</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">As the middle-aged mom walks up to check out, the cashier tells her that she would look like Kate Middleton in the jumpsuit she’s buying, and then asks one of her daughters to look up a picture of Kate Middleton in her orange jumpsuit</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The workers seem to be happy with their jobs and love socializing with the regular customers</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">I start to wonder if the Lutheran mission is something that is important for the workers to agree with</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are plenty of religious objects for sale around the store</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A lot of home signs that say faith, books about Jesus, and even clothing that has religious sayings</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Outside the store, Manchester is very busy and traffic is heavy</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The store is in a strip mall with a butcher shop and is next to a strip mall with an old Hobby Lobby that is now abandoned and an Aldi’s</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There aren’t many cars in the parking lot to any of the stores, but Bethesda’s is the busiest</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The thrift store has two red neon signs on the front and the side of the store facing traffic that says “Bethesda Thrift Shop” in red neon letters</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709328514727.mp4">Video 1</a></p>	m5zMmy4slFNMTuX7a4kn6hIFumX2	38.59281608210409	-90.52975237369537	14646 Manchester Rd, Ballwin, MO 63011, USA	t	f	f	[{"label": "Lutheran", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "shopping", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "thriftstore", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "secondhand", "origin": "user"}]	2019-07-14 17:00:19.961	2024-02-05 19:49:27.875	2025-01-28 18:22:11.893	\N
