65bf9c5d1d442f7c715c9b8e	Serpents and Jackals in the UWS 	<div>There was an SUV decorated with emerald, yellow and dark red crystal beads parked on W. 104th street in the upper west side Manhattan. it had two serpents and two jackals on the hood, and two jackals on its roof. It also had flowers inside the car and on the license plate. In Hindu, Buddhist and Jainist framework, the serpent Naga is a semidivine being, half human half cobra. The name Shiva in Hinduism means jackal. In other south Asian tradition, it represent the goddess Kali.</div><div><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707056153553.jpg" style="\n      max-width: 50%;\n      height: auto; /* Maintain aspect ratio */\n      /* Additional CSS properties for sizing */\n    ">&nbsp;<br><br></div><br>	d2v7JCxLlFT9jkQlvayOD4Z3HAL2	\N	\N	\N	t	f	f	[]	2024-01-22 22:35:00	2024-02-04 14:17:01.659	2025-01-28 18:22:11.296	\N
