65b97f9e1d442f7c715c9b85	Crave Coffee House	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706655799842.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190611_CraveCoffeeHouse_Interior_Riley_001.JPG" width="708" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706655829956.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190611_CraveCoffeeHouse_Interior_Riley_002.JPG" width="704" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">When passing by on SLU’s Medical Campus, the Crave Coffeehouse building appears to be a traditional-looking church. Once inside, however, you are met with a blast of cool air from the ceiling fans on the vaulted ceilings and 2000’s music softly playing over the speakers. You notice the modern-looking brick covering all the walls and the tall stained glass windows that pour color into each side of the room. You see the altar at the front of the worship center, with a big wooden cross lit aglow by a warm light behind it. There is a huge curved counter where friendly workers make coffee out of machines that whir loudly. Customers of all different careers and ages drink coffee, converse, and laugh around the room. Crave Coffeehouse provides an atmosphere that defies traditional religious ideologies, starting with its exterior. Groups of all kinds gather at Crave to create a welcoming atmosphere -- whether it is with a Christian motivation or not.</span></p><p><br><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Do customers typically frequent Crave because of the religious undertones, or just because of the coffee/location?</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Do all the workers share Crave’s religious values?</span><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">What does Crave’s typical customer look like/what is their profession?</span><br></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Soft 2000’s music plays over the speakers and echoes throughout the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Barista laughs with customers who are placing their order</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The air smells like coffee beans and pastries&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A blender whirs as a barista adds in ingredients to make a customer’s smoothie</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The door creaks open and clicks shut as a new group of friends/students arrive</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Three large fans are on the ceiling, making cool air flow throughout the whole shop</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Students doing homework at a nearby table make clicking noises as they type on their laptops</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Little snippets of each conversation is picked up from where I’m sitting every few seconds</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Conversations of two different groups of girls blend together, drone out the music&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sound of the refrigerator whirring is one of the three most prevalent sounds (fridge, music, conversation)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The layout of Crave is an exact replica of a church’s worship center, as they hold a Sunday mass here every week</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Banners at the front of the shop read “loved by God, sent to the world” and “Crave Coffeehouse + Reliant Church”</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A cross is the focal point of the room, is displayed in the middle of the altar-area with a backlight making it look like it’s glowing</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Seven tall, pointed stained glass windows on both side walls pour blue, yellow, red, green, and pink into the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Two of the female students in the room softly sing along to the music playing as they write in notebooks</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A machine behind the coffee counter starts up with a loud electric noise</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Silverware and a mug clink together in a woman’s hand as she begins to clear her table</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The brick that covers all four walls seems old and imperfect, some areas of brick being more white than red</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The room is long and narrow, with an altar at the front. The altar is a stage-like area of the front wall that contains the main lit-up cross, four candles and metal candle holders, and a wooden podium&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">At the back right corner of the room is the coffee bar, a huge curved counter where two workers stand near the register, waiting for their next customer</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">At the very back of the room is the restrooms on either side wall, with huge wooden doors between them that lead out to the parking lot</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Without seeing the “Crave Coffeehouse” sign out front, a passerby may believe that this building is just a traditional church</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Once walking inside, you are met with a nice breeze from the ceiling fans on the high ceilings, friendly baristas that greet you, and a very modern-looking church with a coffee bar in the back that seems like it belongs there</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are stairs leading to a door on one side of the altar that leads to the backstage area</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Above the restrooms and the back door, there is a balcony area like a typical church may have</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The balcony area is made of dark wood, and looks like it’s the oldest and most traditional part of the building</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">All different kinds of people are inside: professionals in the middle of their work day, more casual workers with name badges, young students here to study, and groups of friends of all different ages that gather</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Most groups in the room seem to gather in one corner of the room, the environment feels very friendly and welcoming</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709241768200.mp4">Video 1</a></p>	m5zMmy4slFNMTuX7a4kn6hIFumX2	38.622034103672334	-90.2353048324585	3500 Caroline St, St. Louis, MO 63104, USA	t	f	f	[{"label": "coffee", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "food", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "sounds", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "smells", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "architecture", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "Christianity", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "students", "origin": "user"}]	2019-06-11 17:00:07.708	2024-01-30 23:00:46.904	2025-01-28 18:22:07.778	\N
65c655a81d442f7c715c9b9b	Saint Louis University Clocktower	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707496813953.jpg" alt="LRDA_Object_20190611_SaintLouisUniversityClocktower_Clocktower_Riley.JPG" width="646" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sound of the fountain streams shooting into the air and the feeling of the mist splashing onto the surrounding area are senses that come from the most iconic SLU landmark -- the Clocktower. As tour groups pass, new students and parents stare up at the monument and for the first time and see the most popular part of SLU’s campus. Even when the school year is not in session, the Clocktower remains a hub for activity on campus: families, tour and camp groups, children, professionals and blue collar workers of the University pass by the famous fountain on their way to their destination. Passerbys reach out their hand into a stream of water to cool down in the hot day. Some students sit on the concrete steps and bask in the sunlight or do homework, others find a shady spot in the grass behind it. Wherever they find most comfortable, the soothing sounds of the Clocktower fountain is the sound that epitomizes SLU’s campus and culture.</span><br></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">How many people frequent the Clocktower steps in a day?</span><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Besides in the winter, do the fountains ever get turned off?</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Does the fountains being turned off affect the amount of people that come? Or is the location and the actual Clocktower the most appealing part to visitors?</span></p><p><br></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Water from the fountain crashes down onto the pavement and splashes all the way over to the cement amphitheatre steps</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sun beats down from the sky, making the pavement incredibly hot</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The fountains are the loudest noise within the nearby and surrounding area</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Some of the fountain streams reach nearly 20 feet in the air, whereas others only reach around 3 feet</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Sounds of nearby golf carts rumble closer, then grow distant again</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A huge group of children in soccer uniforms walk by, the sounds of high pitched voices having conversations drowns out the fountain for a moment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">An airplane cuts through the sky above</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Tour groups for new students pass by, all admiring the monument that is the Clocktower as they pass by</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Flags on top of Des Peres hall clap in the wind</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The smaller fountain next to the cement steps constantly flows water into a pool at the bottom, the water being an odd shade of green</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">All different groups of people pass by: families, tour groups, camp groups, moms with toddler-age children, moms with college-age children, individuals in professional clothes that work for the University, individuals in t-shirts and shorts that work for the University</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The air smells like flowers and chlorine</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Bugs fly around constantly</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Passerbys reach into the fountain as they walk past, touching the cool water as the sun beats down on them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Many sweaty people jog past</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Students with study supplies walk past, possibly heading to the library or other peaceful spots on campus to get some work done</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">As a cool wind comes in, it seems like the people walking past breathe a sigh of relief with it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Young people on rentable scooters whiz by the fountain</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">It seems as if the Clocktower is a hub, everybody walks past it to get to their destination on campus</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">While students usually find the cement steps to be a good study/work/relaxation spot on campus, it seems that the 82 degree, sunshiney weather is confining them to the shady spots on the lawn in front of Chaifetz Business School</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Another airplane zooms by, flying just above the Coronado to head to the St. Louis Airport</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Some people sit in the benches nearby the Clocktower, still trying to be close to the central hub, but in the cool shade that surrounds it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Water from the fountain beside the cement steps reflects the sunlight off of it onto the blue walls that surround it, creating lines of light that wiggle and move on it, like the reflection off of a pool</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The Clocktower is a rectangular structure with a round clock near the top of it, with a green triangular point at the very top</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Surrounding its base is a cement circle that holds colorful flowers inside of it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Around that is a circle of fountains that shoot lines of water into the air, that eventually fall back down into the grates below it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are four sidewalks that lead into the Clocktower area from other areas of campus</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">On one side of the Clocktower is cement amphitheater-type steps where students usually sit</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">In the middle of those steps is a blue fountain where water falls down a series of steps into the pool at the bottom</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are two sculptures of people sitting on the surrounding cement area</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709241904498.mp4">Video 1</a></p>	m5zMmy4slFNMTuX7a4kn6hIFumX2	38.63655065701312	-90.23680955171585	220 N Spring Ave, St. Louis, MO 63108, USA	t	f	f	[{"label": "water", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "monument", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "architecture", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "public", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "university", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "sound", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "pedestrian", "origin": "user"}]	2019-06-11 17:00:46.089	2024-02-09 16:41:12.958	2024-06-24 21:31:58.139	\N
