664558c60aafd2348a4e2312	Temple 1 Bell	<p>This is the bell tower (Bonsho) at Temple 1. It is customary to announce yourself to the temple's deity. Dr. Green demonstrating how to ring the bell. In developing the VSP interaction for users, we are lookin at an animation of the bell ringing action as users stop at the bell tower.</p><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732500659488.mp4">Video 1</a></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.15928	134.5025325	Tsukahana-126 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0230, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 00:51:33.084	2024-05-16 00:52:22.809	2024-11-25 02:16:23.928	\N
6641cf4bd0cdb28c4794b665	Shinto shrine - Walk to Temple 2	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732498787893.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="954" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333"><p>Walking henro can encounter many instances of lived religion along the routes between temples, such as this small Shinto shrine on a quiet residential street between Temple 1 and Temple 2. These shrines are generally well-kept, and often have recent offerings.</p><p><br></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.15528248696099	134.4933938783043	Michinokita-38-2 Ōasachōhinoki, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0225, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-13 08:28:03.3	2024-05-13 08:28:59.145	2024-11-25 01:58:39.585	\N
664550905eba0abd4716ab25	Green Line Start - Bando Station	<p>This small train station is the main starting point for the "Green Line," a green painted line on the pavement guiding henro (pilgrims) from the station to the main gate of Ryozen-ji, Temple No. 1 on the Shikoku Pilgrimage. Henro in their white gear are a common sight on the local trains coming from Tokushima Station, especially during the spring pilgrimage season.</p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1556817	134.5069409	Tsujimidō-69 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0232, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 00:16:50.843	2024-05-16 00:17:20.764	2024-09-16 18:01:33.929	\N
66455d5d5eba0abd4716ab27	Temple 1 Daishido	<div>Kobold Daishi hall</div>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1592757	134.5026082	Tsukahana-126 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0230, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 01:11:28.372	2024-05-16 01:11:57.529	2024-06-21 20:55:20.817	\N
664551ca5eba0abd4716ab26	Green Line - Street 	<p>In this semi-rural area, there is a fairly small, but dense mostly residential area between Bando Station and the main gate to Temple 1. The Green Line follows the edge of several streets, with very little room between the street and building fronts.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732676048255.jpg" alt="20240516_092036.jpg" loading="lazy" width="620" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1570106	134.5054619	Hōjō-48-1 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0237, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 00:21:40.625	2024-05-16 00:22:34.309	2024-12-02 02:50:32.333	\N
