66455e495eba0abd4716ab28	Temple 1 bridge	<p>The courtyard at Ryozenji (Temple 1) features a koi pond bounded on two sides by bridge.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733106360780.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="721" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1591932	134.5025826	Tsukahana-126 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0230, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 01:15:02.215	2024-05-16 01:15:53.304	2024-12-02 02:26:46.167	\N
66455ebd0aafd2348a4e2313	Temple 1 gravel path	<div>sounds of gravel</div>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1592498	134.5025093	Tsukahana-126 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0230, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 01:16:16.73	2024-05-16 01:17:49.726	2024-11-22 17:38:28.35	\N
664ab0ef5eba0abd4716ab2f	Temple 14 - Stone slab	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732736634139.jpg" alt="20240520_113157.jpg" loading="lazy" width="763" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p>The main buildings of Temple 14 (Jorakuji) are built on a large stone slab. This temple's principal deity is Miroku Bosatsu. While the temple courtyard, with the exposed stone all around, has an open feel, it is nestled against the mountainside behind it and also maintains a secluded atmosphere.</p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0502323	134.4762795	Enmei-606 Kokufuchō, Tokushima, 779-3128, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-20 02:08:55.918	2024-05-20 02:09:51.378	2024-12-02 02:06:07.573	\N
664815110aafd2348a4e2319	Temple 7 journey-Way marker	<div>wooden way marker</div>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.119384	134.3828586	Miyanohigashi-43 Hikino, Kamiita, Itano District, Tokushima 771-1311, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-18 02:39:37.256	2024-05-18 02:40:17.525	2024-11-22 17:37:05.417	\N
66458b0e8aad2c5255e531e0	Way marker- Journey to Temple 3	<p>One small, but important detail about the journey between temples for the walking henro are the way markers that are placed along the route most commonly used. These markers come in a variety of forms, with older wooden and stone markers mixed with laminated paper sheets and even painted markers on the ground or a nearby object (such as a guardrail).</p><p></p><p>With modern access to smartphone navigation, we observed many henro using their phones, but as our team traced the route between Temple 2 and Temple 3 on foot ourselves we found we often needed the way markers we encountered to verify we were on the path to the next temple.</p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1501106	134.4852816	Ashitani-2-2 Kawabata, Itano, Itano District, Tokushima 779-0102, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 04:26:26.303	2024-05-16 04:26:54.555	2024-06-21 20:55:24.212	\N
664579470aafd2348a4e2316	Temple 2 temizuya	<p>Gokurakuji (Temple 2) temizuya, or washing station for visitors to cleanse themselves before proceeding into further into the temple precinct.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733106229486.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="675" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1556842	134.4907857	Dannoue-12 Ōasachōhinoki, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0225, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 03:10:24.724	2024-05-16 03:11:03.211	2024-12-02 02:24:29.718	\N
