6645834a0aafd2348a4e2317	Temple 2 - Daishido	<p>The Daishido at Temple 2 is located adjacent to the Hondo, or mail hall on a narrow terrace above the rest of the temple complex. The Daishido can be reached either via a set of steep stairs, made of stone and concrete, or a concrete ramp that begins along the edge of the temple space at the back of the lower area and curves more gently around up to the back of the Daishido.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733105958785.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="676" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p></p><p>During our field visit, a tour group led by a Zen Buddhist monk was visiting the temple, and recited the sutras at the hondo and daishido before leaving fairly quickly. The monk stopped for a moment to say hello, before following after the tour group. Some members of the group had portions of the henro attire, but others were dressed in casual clothing. Groups that travel to temples on the pilgrimage via bus are common, and it is an acceptable way to participate.&nbsp;</p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1557446	134.490477	Dannoue-12 Ōasachōhinoki, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0225, Japan	t	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 03:53:25.147	2024-05-16 03:53:46.465	2024-12-02 02:48:05.215	\N
