66480d045eba0abd4716ab2e	Temple 6 pagoda	<p>Anrakuji's two-storey pagoda is difficult to photograph in the small, enclosed space of the temple grounds, and is partially hidden by trees. </p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733105552600.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="725" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333"><p><br></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1180521	134.3889031	Teranonishikita-5 Hikino, Kamiita, Itano District, Tokushima 771-1311, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-18 02:05:19.96	2024-05-18 02:05:56.786	2024-12-02 02:13:13.938	\N
664b21323a48ef5557d2b71d	Happy Science encounter	<div>While returning on the train from Temple 16 to Tokushima Station, I was engaged in conversation with a small group of visitors who asked if I spoke English. When I responded yes, an Austalian man began to speak with me, telling me he was part of a religious group called Happy Science, and he and his companions were in Shikoku to attend a retreat with their organization.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><br></div>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0745888	134.5510927	1-chōme-61 Terashimahonchōnishi, Tokushima, 770-0831, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-20 10:04:13.112	2024-05-20 10:08:50.38	2024-11-22 17:36:48.771	\N
664c49400aafd2348a4e231c	Temple 23 - Rail journey	<p>Tokushima to Hiwasa - Trip is just under two hours by rail, passing through the city of Anan and a number of small towns.The train was quiet, but there were several other henro in their gear traveling to Temple 23 as well. </p><p></p><p></p><p><br></p><p>Temples 20-22, are not easily accessible by rail and can be hiked to via Temple 19 or starting from Tatsue Station on the JR Mugi Line. For this field work, the team is focusing on temples that can be accessed by public transit, with shorter walks in between, to maximize our visits. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	33.9217662	134.659438	Tonomachi-12番地3 Tomiokachō, Anan, Tokushima 774-0030, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-21 07:08:53.409	2024-05-21 07:12:00.031	2024-11-27 01:45:54.694	\N
664e7c428aad2c5255e531ec	Tokushima-Wakayama Nankai Ferry	<div>When henro complete their journey, or wish to visit Kukai's resting place, they will travel to Mount Koya, or Koyasan.</div><div><br></div><div>There are a number of ways to get from Shikoku to Koyasan. The Wakayama Nankai Ferry takes passengers back to Honshu just south of Osaka, and then travelers can take a train to the foot of Mount Koya.&nbsp;</div>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0606904	134.5965169	2-chōme-26-12 Higashiokinosu, Tokushima, 770-0873, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-22 23:09:32.604	2024-05-22 23:14:10.669	2024-11-22 17:35:06.593	\N
669ffc34e204d96d2b864dba	Crave Coffee	<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">When passing by on SLU’s Medical Campus, the Crave Coffeehouse building appears to be a traditional-looking church. Once inside, however, you are met with a blast of cool air from the ceiling fans on the vaulted ceilings and 2000’s music softly playing over the speakers. You notice the modern-looking brick covering all the walls and the tall stained glass windows that pour color into each side of the room. You see the altar at the front of the worship center, with a big wooden cross lit aglow by a warm light behind it. There is a huge curved counter where friendly workers make coffee out of machines that whir loudly. Customers of all different careers and ages drink coffee, converse, and laugh around the room. Crave Coffeehouse provides an atmosphere that defies traditional religious ideologies, starting with its exterior. Groups of all kinds gather at Crave to create a welcoming atmosphere -- whether it is with a Christian motivation or not.</span></p><p style="text-align: start"><br><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Do customers typically frequent Crave because of the religious undertones, or just because of the coffee/location?</span></p><p style="text-align: start"></p><p style="text-align: start"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Do all the workers share Crave’s religious values?</span></p><p style="text-align: start"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">What does Crave’s typical customer look like/what is their profession?</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Soft 2000’s music plays over the speakers and echoes throughout the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Barista laughs with customers who are placing their order</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The air smells like coffee beans and pastries&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A blender whirs as a barista adds in ingredients to make a customer’s smoothie</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The door creaks open and clicks shut as a new group of friends/students arrive</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Three large fans are on the ceiling, making cool air flow throughout the whole shop</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Students doing homework at a nearby table make clicking noises as they type on their laptops</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Little snippets of each conversation is picked up from where I’m sitting every few seconds</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Conversations of two different groups of girls blend together, drone out the music&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sound of the refrigerator whirring is one of the three most prevalent sounds (fridge, music, conversation)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The layout of Crave is an exact replica of a church’s worship center, as they hold a Sunday mass here every week</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Banners at the front of the shop read “loved by God, sent to the world” and “Crave Coffeehouse + Reliant Church”</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A cross is the focal point of the room, is displayed in the middle of the altar-area with a backlight making it look like it’s glowing</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Seven tall, pointed stained glass windows on both side walls pour blue, yellow, red, green, and pink into the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Two of the female students in the room softly sing along to the music playing as they write in notebooks</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A machine behind the coffee counter starts up with a loud electric noise</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Silverware and a mug clink together in a woman’s hand as she begins to clear her table</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The brick that covers all four walls seems old and imperfect, some areas of brick being more white than red</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The room is long and narrow, with an altar at the front. The altar is a stage-like area of the front wall that contains the main lit-up cross, four candles and metal candle holders, and a wooden podium&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">At the back right corner of the room is the coffee bar, a huge curved counter where two workers stand near the register, waiting for their next customer</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">At the very back of the room is the restrooms on either side wall, with huge wooden doors between them that lead out to the parking lot</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Without seeing the “Crave Coffeehouse” sign out front, a passerby may believe that this building is just a traditional church</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Once walking inside, you are met with a nice breeze from the ceiling fans on the high ceilings, friendly baristas that greet you, and a very modern-looking church with a coffee bar in the back that seems like it belongs there</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are stairs leading to a door on one side of the altar that leads to the backstage area</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Above the restrooms and the back door, there is a balcony area like a typical church may have</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The balcony area is made of dark wood, and looks like it’s the oldest and most traditional part of the building</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">All different kinds of people are inside: professionals in the middle of their work day, more casual workers with name badges, young students here to study, and groups of friends of all different ages that gather</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Most groups in the room seem to gather in one corner of the room, the environment feels very friendly and welcomin</span></p></li></ul>	mPpZp21UPnZSqevTcExeLXCxhfP2	38.6364364	-90.2362638	JQP7+HF St. Louis, MO, USA	f	f	f	[{"label": "Christianity", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "testing", "origin": "user"}]	2024-07-23 18: