674e0ed0deae4d162f083a7a	Temple 3 to 4 path - Small temple	<p>The common pathway connecting Temple 3 (<em>Konsenji</em>) and Temple 4 (<em>Dainichiji</em>) transitions from paved roads to a scenic route that winds through small fields, wooded areas, and tranquil bamboo groves. Along the way, it passes through a small, unaffiliated temple before rejoining a paved street.</p><p></p><p>At this unaffiliated temple, the resident monk often extends warm hospitality to passing <em>henro</em> (pilgrims), offering refreshments and engaging in friendly conversation when he is at home. This welcoming gesture adds a personal and heartwarming touch to the pilgrimage, creating a moment of connection and respite amidst the sacred journey.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733168719238.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="485" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75 / 1">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	\N	\N	\N	t	f	f	[]	2024-12-02 19:41:52.699	2024-12-02 19:47:28.486	2025-03-18 18:12:30.422	\N
674f4cf038f26c9105983664	Itano Station - Henro guide	<p>Itano Station, located on the JR Shikoku Kōtoku Line, is the nearest local train station to Temple 3 (<em>Konsenji</em>), Temple 4 (<em>Dainichiji</em>), and Temple 5 (<em>Jizōji</em>) on the Shikoku Pilgrimage. This station serves as a convenient access point for pilgrims traveling by train to these temples.</p><p></p><p>Notably, someone has thoughtfully placed informational literature on the Shikoku Pilgrimage in English beneath the train schedule, offering valuable guidance to international pilgrims. This gesture reflects the welcoming spirit of the pilgrimage and provides an accessible resource for understanding the journey’s significance and practical details, even for those unfamiliar with Japanese.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733250183108.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="722" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.14169	134.464716	Itano Station-minami, Ōji Ōtera, Itano, Itano District, Tokushima 779-0105, Japan	t	f	f	[]	2024-12-03 18:12:59.376	2024-12-03 18:24:48.332	2025-03-18 18:14:06.519	\N
674f498adeae4d162f083a7b	Waymarker - Temple 3 to 4 Path	<p>This laminated, printed waymarker is one of many that guide pilgrims along the pathways in Tokushima Prefecture, serving as a helpful navigation aid throughout the Shikoku Pilgrimage. With the growing participation of non-Japanese pilgrims, newer printed markers increasingly feature bilingual text in both English and Japanese, making the pilgrimage more accessible to international travelers.</p><p></p><p>These waymarkers are not only practical tools but also visible symbols of the pilgrimage experience, blending tradition with modern inclusivity as they guide pilgrims on their sacred journey.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733248224381.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="652" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75 / 1">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.14774902334756	134.47185922568664	Sōtokuden-71-1 Kawabata, Itano, Itano District, Tokushima 779-0102, Japan	t	f	f	[]	2024-12-03 17:47:59.274	2024-12-03 18:10:18.673	2025-03-18 18:22:51.877	\N
6750b2f6bcb8fa58966853dd	Waymarker - Temple 14 to 15 journey	<p>This is an example of the more substantial stone markers erected along the henro route in Tokushima prefecture.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733341875915.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="499" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0497625888544	134.47656018783573	Nishiyano-780 Kokufuchō, Tokushima, 779-3127, Japan	t	f	f	[]	2024-12-04 19:48:18.251	2024-12-04 19:52:22.267	2025-03-18 18:20:56.07	\N
