678029271132ef2b3c8f1d15	Cathedral, Basilica of St. Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736452314648.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1320" style="aspect-ratio: 0.460251 / 1"><p><br></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736452323122.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1320" style="aspect-ratio: 0.460251 / 1"><p><br></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736452344243.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1320" style="aspect-ratio: 0.460251 / 1"><p><br></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736452356765.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1320" style="aspect-ratio: 0.460251 / 1"><p><br></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736452379936.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1320" style="aspect-ratio: 0.460251 / 1"><p>The Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis is a remarkable structure with a complex build. From the outside you see a grand window, a castle like gothic design, arched doors, and a traditional Roman approach to style. The grass is vibrant green with trees that blow in the wind and overhang onto the building. The church bells ring loud for anyone near to hear and you listen to a soft mumble of conversations as visitors slowly make their way up the steps. Upon entering the church, you are greeted with the smell of incense and burning candles for those who have lit one in remembrance, or in prayer, of a loved one. The piano music plays at the perfect volume and encompasses the sacred area in a serene way as it echoes through the walls. The atmosphere is stunning with breathtaking meticulous mosaics filled with vibrant colors and exhibiting displays from the bible. Marble columns line the long hallways that form a path to the alter, where you see Jesus Christ hung from a cross, surrounded by exquisite and majestic architecture. As I sit in the pew I have chosen, my hands caress the cold polished wood, and I embody all of the wonderful things that are surrounding me. I look around and see fellow worshippers who have also chosen to be here in this place of worship on this beautiful Sunday. I see them gathered together, singing, kneeling in prayer, greeting those around them, and preparing for mass to begin.</p><p></p><p>Every time I step foot into this cathedral, I always feel something different. A sense of admiration, and devotion always fills my body, but the feeling on why I show up each Sunday feels a little different as I grow in my faith. To be a part of something so substantial and so connected to Jesus gives me a feeling of contentment. When I see others gathered to worship the same God and to give their selves and their prayers to Christ to take hold of, it instills a feeling of shared community and togetherness. What is happening within the walls feels harmonious and divine, like no one can disturb you in this time of worship, as if time stands still for a moment. The cathedral brings to us a place of preservation for our traditions and a place to practice our beliefs.</p><p></p><p>The Cathedral Basilica is a true representation of a framework that converges various topics into one. With its depictions of faith, history, stories, and craftsmanship, it serves as a true indication of what Catholic institutions are meant to symbolize and preserves its legacy for forthcoming communities.</p><p></p><p>Questions:</p><p>Are the mosaics meant to show specific occurrences from the bible, or are they more so meant to be open to interpretation?</p><p></p><p>How is the placement of the Cathedral Basilica important to its religious ties as a sacred house of worship? Does St. Louis signify something special for it?</p><p></p><p>When the cathedral was built, do you think that it came with the intention that the people who enter through its holy doors, may not be religious, but instead simply tourists who are interested in its history and architecture?</p>	rdhZC6H9O1bzb92yPQMyCM8WbPO2	38.66205925614059	-90.29577606558367	6124 Horton Pl, St. Louis, MO 63133, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-01-09 19:53:11.122	2025-01-09 19:53:11.414	2025-01-09 20:44:29.611	\N
