68269b1acfd83da30865d4de	Noted German Artist Coming Here to Decorate Cathedral- The Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfXNaCwcX7V5TcJ59mkD5y-Ci_RVmggufFJhTV4eQrykI984MfqWxAmSQTjFulHqzh3fvM5dLuzZGZAOtXHpqynmxiReCDqN2n5T16sH_RhbJeSaX4NRW6JHLTC2o5s4RAUIWuxxQ?key=3MsIV_IskFe34Z10TxtHMZmP" loading="lazy" width="283" style="aspect-ratio: 0.448125"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">This newspaper column states that August Oetgen, a well known mosaic artist in Germany, will be making the trip to St. Louis to assist in the installation of the mosaics at the cathedral. The lengths the architects, artists, and Catholic officials went to making sure these mosaics were beautiful and well made shows that these mosaics were important and meant to be impactful.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Title: Noted German Artist Coming Here to Decorate Cathedral&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Creator: Associated Press</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Publisher: The Post-Dispatch St. Louis</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Contributor: Maura Hill&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Date: October 22nd, 1923</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Type: Newspaper</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Format: Page 1</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Rights: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Newspaper.com"><span style="color: rgb(17, 85, 2