68269b1acfd83da30865d4dd	Legions of Catholics to March To Cathedral Site- The Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdNbiOOs3DMtOc6KaPrcGgKpya5Am-YXcyrYBcuu82K_xkP3pD20uEbtsrkdf9FzZJHh2x88IXcsMfGy7NWxQphmM3ryZpc3R_cjl25WWAQCR3YAMqd0b2EeIXYVyjOIdmJLJ-E2w?key=3MsIV_IskFe34Z10TxtHMZmP" loading="lazy" width="302" style="aspect-ratio: 0.611875"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">This newspaper article briefly discusses the parade that took place at the laying of the cornerstone of the cathedral. Thousands of people and over fifty musicians attended the parade. This kind of celebration is rarely seen today and indicates the impact this new church had on the community even in the early stages of construction.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Title: Legions of Catholics to March to Cathedral Site</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Creator: Unknown</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Publisher: The Post-Dispatch St. Louis&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Contributor: Maura Hill</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Date: October 11th, 1908</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Type: Newspaper</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Format: Page 20</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Rights: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Newspaper.com"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Newspaper.com</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Source: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Newspaper.com"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Newspaper.com</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt"> , The Post-Dispatch St. Louis, MO</span></p><p><br></p>	zHwslkIPrdaiaeuXvaSbHh0JIHt1	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	[]	2025-05-16 01:55:13.921	2025-05-16 01:55:38.906	2025-05-16 05:03:15.584	\N
68269b1acfd83da30865d4dc	Building St. Louis' Great Cathedral- The Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdNceDau1J3P0C6W9nZ59CB4sSPO1NTBiJqn6JHzlg4HIJBEorRc6dcvISu_u-LGtZ1n3HKX0NgW53KoSSZRKqXbSkTA70_zKh_BHQ5AgcsU2ewXf63lixSY5Khb6xOrjL0Q4X1XA?key=3MsIV_IskFe34Z10TxtHMZmP" loading="lazy" width="295" style="aspect-ratio: 0.855625"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Two weeks after the previous article, an entire page of the Post dispatch was dedicated to the excitement surrounding the start of this amazing building. An illustration shows us an image of what the cathedral was planned to look like after its completion. From this drawing, it is clear there is art on the ceilings in some areas, but it is unclear if the copious amounts of mosaics were a part of the plan at this time. This article showcases the excitement and impact of this cathedral and also brings up the question of when the mosaic route was taken.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Title: Building St. Louis’ Great Cathedral</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Creator: Rev D. S. Phelan&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Publisher: The Post Dispatch St. Louis</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Contributor: Maura Hill&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Date: November 11th, 1908</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Type: Newspaper</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Format: Page 49</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Rights: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Newspaper.com"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Newspaper.com</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Source: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Newspaper.com"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Newspaper.com</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt"> , The Post-Dispatch St. Louis, MO</span></p><p><br></p>	zHwslkIPrdaiaeuXvaSbHh0JIHt1	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	[]	2025-05-16 01:55:13.921	2025-05-16 01:55:38.843	2025-05-16 05:04:25.442	\N
68269b1acfd83da30865d4da	Vestibule Memorial to Msgr. Tannrath Is Opened to View- The Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfjTiGU5YtTPiV2A98n4fLeVzQU3cLoi9qE467s952P_REXLY54nDX2eK84ZDFt092NuF5x0E9xwkmEeevvCg0vDxQZJRWZ7lFsfBrVXhJgXH9Nx3sJkDUSvk9CAvsY0-IYfG1H5Q?key=3MsIV_IskFe34Z10TxtHMZmP" loading="lazy" width="366" style="aspect-ratio: 0.560625"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The left-most column and top photo on this page of a newspaper discuss the memorial mosaic created for Msgr. J. J. Tannrath. The creation of a memorial mosaic showcases that these pieces of art carry weight for the community and are more than beautiful images, but a story of faith as well the specific St. Louis Catholic community.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Title: Vestibule Memorial to Msgr. Tannrath is Opened to View</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Creator: Unknown</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Publisher: St. Louis Globe Democrat</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Contributor: Maura Hill&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Date: June 29th, 1931</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Type: Newspaper</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Format: Page 3</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Rights: Unknown</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Source: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://