6827d70b56ac5d90d588ccf8	Front Facade	<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt">The Hindu Temple of St. Louis is the largest Hindu place of worship in the St. Louis area. The temple got its start in 1988 when it was registered as a not for profit organization in the State of Missouri. In 1991 the main temple was completed. The deity sculptures were installed in 1995. There are around 14,000 Hindu practitioners living in the St. Louis area. The goal of this documentation project is to document and record the various features of the temple on separate notes on the Where’s Religion website.</span></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1747441280676.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="314" style="aspect-ratio: 1.32198 / 1"><p>"The Temple was first registered as a not for profit organization in the state of Missouri on March 7th, 1988" (Temple History). Construction was finished and services began on Nov 8, 1991. The temple is one of Seven official Hindu organizations in the St. Louis area.</p><p></p><p>Hindu Temple of St. Louis, Mark Lovelace, YouTube, Blake Koehr, Image, JPEG, Hindu Temple of St. Louis website. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.hindutemplestlouis.org/temple-history/">https://www.hindutemplestlouis.org/temple-history/</a></p>	oZd2tbTqLhhKlzxSGPW7ic6F1Pv2	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	[]	2025-05-16 22:54:50.498	2025-05-17 00:23:39.748	2025-05-17 00:52:25.726	\N
