65c572675d508d3d84952105	Goodwill Religion	<p>Thrift stores often sell donated and discarded items that can be classified as “religion.” Some of these items, like the Buddha below, were originally marketed as household decor in a home goods store, or the woodcarvings of indigenous people in full ceremonial dress. The Bible verse coffee mug might have had a more intentionally devotional intention among its past (and perhaps future) users. Figurines, whether for holiday or year-long display, can fall into either of these categories (and others). </p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707437230377.jpg"><p></p><p></p><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707437257783.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707437274399.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707437329412.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707437399788.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707438015695.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707438045296.jpg"><p><br><br></p><p><br></p>	8H86gZYSFIRHGy8q39OgBAfQFeC2	38.62467900445431	-90.3476442121387	1909 S Brentwood Blvd, Brentwood, MO 63144, USA	t	f	f	[]	2024-02-09 00:06:42.866	2024-02-09 00:31:35.425	2024-12-07 21:00:04.642	\N
