nsparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span></span></p><ul style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Greek Language Program</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Byzantine Choir</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Grief and Bereavement Support Group</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Recipe Club</span></p><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><br></p><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><br></p></li></ul><p dir="ltr" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><b>Hofstra Religious Mapping Fieldwork Notes</b></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Dr. Burlein</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The most notable aspect of our visit was the physical space itself. Every inch of the temple (they reserve the word ‘church’ for the people) is covered in mosaics: on one side, Mary and her life story, on the other side that of St. Paul; behind the altar is the resurrection and in the dome is Jesus as sustainer of the world. There is a side altar for venerating three icons (two of Mary and one of St. Nicholas) which wept myrrh; the icons are removed and processed on special days. To the side there is a small chapel of St. Anastasia, who is associated with healing through potions and elixirs. This chapel also houses a number of relics, including two of its patron St. Paul.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&nbsp;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">There are two priests, for 750 families. Divine liturgy is said predominantly in English (about 80%), with the remainder in Greek. Roughly 500-600 people attend the Divine Liturgy on any given Sunday, after which there is a coffee hour. There are approximately 150 sacraments or life cycle events (births, marriages, and deaths) celebrated each year.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&nbsp;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Each Greek Orthodox community develops its own unique expression of service. At St. Paul’s, this takes the following forms: 1) a special liturgy for people with disabilities or illness; 2) Love Delivered, formed by the young adults who get together maybe four times a year to cook and freeze food, which is then delivered to people who are ill; 3)</span><a href="https://nam04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmidnightrun.org%2F&amp;data=05%7C01%7CASine3%40pride.hofstra.edu%7Ce4acd7c485244a6c1db708db5bce3599%7Ce32fc43d7c6246d9b49fcd53ba8d9424%7C0%7C0%7C638204713452334167%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=%2Fh0nGp%2FLignCD8Z14CpKdqWQ6%2Fi7buMXPZJW5zBRslg%3D&amp;reserved=0" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Midnight Run</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">; and 4) volunteering with</span><a href="https://nam04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthe-inn.org%2F&amp;data=05%7C01%7CASine3%40pride.hofstra.edu%7Ce4acd7c485244a6c1db708db5bce3599%7Ce32fc43d7c6246d9b49fcd53ba8d9424%7C0%7C0%7C638204713452334167%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=djABDDPi7qJej9hViEWXN9u%2FwzXmT1DWLZlALRxo%2F0w%3D&amp;reserved=0" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Mary Brennan INN</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> soup kitchen.&nbsp; While the website still lists a Cancer Support group and Homebound Ministries, those are currently inactive.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><b id="docs-internal-guid-e21fb843-7fff-a3f9-dce3-d179f0540d23" style="caret-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3); -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: normal;"><br></b></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">During covid, there was some controversy around communion. In Orthodoxy, Communion the bread and wine are believed to become the Body and Blood of Christ; as the purest substance that there is, the belief was that the practice of receiving Communion would not transmit contagion.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span><br class="Apple-interchange-newline" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Andrew</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Father Elias was very welcoming and was eager to engage in dialogue with the community about Orthodoxy. He encouraged us to ask questions. His explanations of the traditions of Greek Orthodox (such as the importance of the icons as windows to the divine) were very engaging and easy to understand. Father Elias expressed interest in reaching out to the surrounding community to engage in dialogue whether it is in an interfaith context, or any other.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-d5789c84-7fff-ddf2-68a2-fe63151afced" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span><br class="Apple-interchange-newline" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times, serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap;"><b>Dr. Julie Byrne</b></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times, serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap;">Fr. Elias gave us a tour of the nave and side chapel of St. Anastasia, and then we sat in the nave for more conversation.&nbsp; Memorable topics throughout the 1.5-hour convo included:&nbsp;</span><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-color: transparent; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span id="docs-internal-guid-9c017083-7fff-0952-88b6-8087a9b64015" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span></span></p><ul style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">the sanctuary is off-limits to all but priests and those assisting priests, the latter of whom can be lay women or men, who receive a blessing in order to enter;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">communion is limited to those baptized and chrismated in Orthodoxy, but there is a taking of unblessed elements at the end of the service for anyone who is a baptized Christian;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">miraculous icons and relics are a somewhat “normal” phenomenon in the Orthodox community, meaning quite common; the formerly weeping icons in a shrine to the right of the sanctuary attract people on a daily basis to come and sit quietly and pray, and the cathedral accommodates this by inviting people to ring the bell and they will be let in during business hours;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">the St. Paul community began in Astoria, then Hempstead, and has since then “seeded” about eight other Orthodox locations in the tristate area since its move to Cathedral Street;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">the organization of Orthodoxy worldwide, with the center of the US jurisdictions in Istanbul with Europe, North America and South America considered “foreign lands” per the ancient ecumenical councils; attempted continued modern fidelity to the ancient ecumenical councils;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Orthodoxy is growing in the US but exhibits the usual “gap” in age participation of college-age people (for which Fr. Elias faulted “us priests” when they emphasize rules and regulations over a personal relationship with Christ);&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">the spread of Orthodoxy worldwide, including in sub-Saharan Africa and New Zealand; evangelization takes the form of setting up missions in places where there is none nearby with a priest who just “does [their] thing” and slowly gathers a community;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Times, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">the story of Fr. Elias’s own path to the priesthood; discussion of the options for marriage for Orthodox priests and celibacy for bishops.&nbsp; </span></p></li></ul><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span><span id="docs-internal-guid-137996ed-7fff-0b53-35bf-284acc54febd" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span><br class="Apple-interchange-newline" style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.847); white-space: normal; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);"></span></p><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><br></p></span>	QLzutEofUsO5JNKCsMdZSNGFZ0P2	-73.846146	40.681938	2HR25M3J+GQ	f	f	f	[]	2024-02-28 18:17:38.746	2024-02-28 18:34:12.708	2024-06-21 20:54:40.964	\N
