662bf9a85cc3848690279fb9	Christmakah in Southern California	<p>This Southern California family takes a break from the Church of Baseball to honor their family traditions through Christmakah. They eat potato latkes dressed in a manner common among the Levey clan of south Texas - an applesauce base is topped with cherry preserves and sour cream. They light the Hanukkah candles and dance around the coffee table as they play the Barenaked Ladies' version of "Hanukkah o' Hanukkah." The glow of lights from the Christmas tree complement the candles to bathe the room in  the light of the season. </p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1714157914705.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="2252" style="aspect-ratio: 0.5606173761513568"><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1714157914698.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="4032" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333"><p></p><p></p>	to6gNGICQ1X1EHBDN6KQVeykKas2	\N	\N	\N	t	f	f	[]	2024-04-26 18:55:36.574	2024-04-26 18:59:52.157	2024-06-21 20:54:18.886	\N
