66391b41d0cdb28c4794b5fc	Wat Thung Luang	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1715018384441.jpg" alt="Wat Thung Luang .008.JPG" loading="lazy" width="616" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333"><p>Three images by Sala Khaek in background. Principle image and two gilded attendant images.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1715018463269.jpg" alt="Wat Thung Luang .010.JPG" loading="lazy" width="451" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><p>Principle image detail.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1715018493807.jpg" alt="Wat Thung Luang .011.JPG" loading="lazy" width="477" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><p>Attendant image right.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1715018539886.jpg" alt="Wat Thung Luang .013.JPG" loading="lazy" width="466" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><p>Attendant image left.</p>	mvYjmNueigWqx1hs4tP3RvX7IUG2	19.974787576469353	99.76408152016903	XQF7+WJ8, Mae Yao, Mueang Chiang Rai District, Chiang Rai 57100, Thailand	f	f	f	[{"label": "SalaKhaek", "origin": "user"}]	2024-05-06 17:54:38.77	2024-05-06 18:02:41.351	2024-06-21 20:54:33.49	\N
664fe2983a48ef5557d2b729	Okunuin cemetery - Kobodaishi Mausoleum entrance 	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732733773797.jpg" alt="IMG_2583.jpg" loading="lazy" width="759" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p>This is the most well-known and largest cemetery in Japan, located at Mount Koya or Koyasan. The cemetery has over 200,000 graves, including emperors, samurai lords, monks, and members of many prominent Japanese families. At the heart of the cemetery, and the end of a nearly 2km long path, is the mausoleum of Kukai, posthumously given the title of Kobo Daishi.The cemetery' setting in old-growth forest, with the long central pathway shaded even during the day, gives Okunoin an otherworldly feel, and most visitors remain quiet or speak in soft tones as they move through the grounds.</p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.2176954	135.6047493	6J93+4W, Koyasan, Koya, Ito District, Wakayama 648-0211, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-24 00:37:44.642	2024-05-24 00:43:04.074	2024-12-02 01:46:30.031	\N
