66455d3c8aad2c5255e531df	Temple 1 Pagoda	<p>This is the two-storey pagoda at Temple 1. With the foliage and tight layout of the temple, the pagoda almost blends in with the trees from some angles.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732675874510.jpg" alt="20240516_095510.jpg" loading="lazy" width="502" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1592757	134.5026082	Tsukahana-126 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0230, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 00:52:29.604	2024-05-16 01:11:24.596	2024-11-27 02:51:44.066	\N
664551133a48ef5557d2b718	Green Line - Approach to Temple 1 (Ryozenji)	<p>This is the approach to Temple 1's main gate along the Green Line. As new pilgrims approach, they can go directly through the main gate, or turn right along the temple wall and enter the parking lot to access the Henro store and buy their gear, stamp books, and other items before returning the gate for a formal entry into the temple.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733108950629.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="682" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1565977	134.5071296	Tsujimidō-82-1 Ōasachō Bandō, Naruto, Tokushima 779-0232, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-16 00:19:02.501	2024-05-16 00:19:31.575	2024-12-02 03:09:55.345	\N
66b595e9ae8382984e151252	The Faces Around Mary and Baby Jesus	<p>This can be found walking down a row of restaurants in Hasbrouck I suppose as part of the store front of a shop that sells statues.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1723176364625.jpg" alt="IMG_9275.jpg" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	d2v7JCxLlFT9jkQlvayOD4Z3HAL2	40.6916408	-73.9140959	490a Central Ave, Brooklyn, NY 11221, USA	t	f	f	[]	2024-08-09 04:02:01.708	2024-08-09 04:07:05.512	2026-04-15 13:48:36.955	\N
66c7485fae8382984e1512c9	Catholic Figures Facing the Street in Williamsburg	<p>It's interesting that some of the windowsills in New York City have religious statues facing the street rather than, expectedly, inside the home. For some, it is done to protect the home from vandals and those who wish to harm. For some, it serves to remind the passers by of godliness. </p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1724336208692.jpg" alt="IMG_8951.jpeg" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1724336208693.jpg" alt="IMG_8952.jpeg" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	d2v7JCxLlFT9jkQlvayOD4Z3HAL2	40.7081156	-73.9570696	315 Broadway, Brooklyn, NY 11211, USA	t	f	f	[]	2024-08-22 14:14:04.729	2024-08-22 14:17:03.248	2026-04-15 13:48:37.07	\N
