674d2c4342f3d7d7c4471375	Temple 5 - Statue	<p>Each temple on the Shikoku Pilgrimage features a statue of Kūkai (Kōbō Daishi), honoring the revered founder of Shingon Buddhism and the pilgrimage itself. This particular statue, located at Temple 5 (<em>Jizōji</em>), exemplifies the profound respect and devotion that Kūkai inspires among pilgrims. These statues serve not only as symbols of his enduring spiritual legacy but also as focal points for reflection and prayer along the sacred journey.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733110594952.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="560" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75 / 1">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	[]	2024-12-02 03:35:01.241	2024-12-02 03:40:51.157	2024-12-03 20:37:49.496	\N
