6942e973ba8e50e22cd4ffcd	Dog Park Rosary	Plastic bag with note posted by patron or staff at dog park containing a rosary found in the grass.Dog parks can be spaces where people of different religions, political affiliations, races, and other cultural identities gather. Many faith traditions also have special blessings for pets as they increasingly become part of social lives of families and communities.Was this rosary brought to the park for a specific ritual? Was it merely on a person while they were there? While it may not be possible to know all the circumstances of this religious object, it does prompt questions about how we can better understand religion in unexpected public spaces as insights to religion in modern life.<img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1765992747166.jpg"><br>	8H86gZYSFIRHGy8q39OgBAfQFeC2	38.610685616653505	-90.4881473868304	JG66+7P Town and Country, MO, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-12-17 17:33:39.129	2025-12-17 17:33:39.374	2026-04-15 13:48:42.06	\N
682597d863707c94a6aad4a4	Lithograph of St. Louis Cathedral, 1840	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1747294165338.jpg" loading="lazy" width="507" style="aspect-ratio: 1.4607703281027105"><p></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif">Pictured is a lithograph of the grounds of the Old Cathedral, to the right pictures the Bishop’s House. The Cathedral is the only remaining original structure from the time. There are buildings in the background, none of which are standing today, placed where the interstate is now carved through downtown St. Louis.</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Title: </strong><em>St. Louis Cathedral</em> Published and Lithographed by J.C. Wild</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Author: </strong>J.C. Wild</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Publisher:</strong> J.C. Wild</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Contributor: </strong>Kathleen Jochman</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Format: </strong>JPG image 238 x 288</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif"><strong>Rights:</strong> No Known Copyright</span></p><p><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt"><strong>Source: </strong></span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://mohistory.org/collections/item/N29570"><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif">https://mohistory.org/collections/item/N29570</span></a><span>&nbsp;</span><br></p>	TrWZ9PxTspOnzWwVD6UeQTxC5s12	38.62403143856819	-90.18733430065917	209 Walnut St, St. Louis, MO 63102, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-05-15 07:29:28.424	2025-05-15 07:29:28.843	2025-05-16 01:52:59.565	\N
