6827e3b763707c94a6aad4c6	Vaikasi Vikasam	<p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt">The Hindu Temple of St. Louis is the largest Hindu place of worship in the St. Louis area. The temple got its start in 1988 when it was registered as a not for profit organization in the State of Missouri. In 1991 the main temple was completed. The deity sculptures were installed in 1995. There are around 14,000 Hindu practitioners living in the St. Louis area. The goal of this documentation project is to document and record the various features of the temple on separate notes on the Where’s Religion website.</span></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1747444383909.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="201" style="aspect-ratio: 0.747638326585695"><p>Vaikasi Vikasam, a yearly festival in honor of the Hindu god Lord Murugan.</p><p></p><p>The Hindu Temple of St. Louis, Blake Koehr, Image, JPG, The Hindu Temple of St. Louis, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://hindutemplestlouis.smugmug.com/2019-Photos/Vaikasi-Vishakam">https://hindutemplestlouis.smugmug.com/2019-Photos/Vaikasi-Vishakam</a>.</p><p></p>	oZd2tbTqLhhKlzxSGPW7ic6F1Pv2	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	[]	2025-05-17 01:12:39.152	2025-05-17 01:17:43.338	2026-04-15 13:48:41.393	\N
