64af4b1fa3a722500eabdf93	Epiphany Lanes	Located on the campus of Epiphany of Our Lord Catholic Church, Epiphany Lanes is (as of 2022) a fully functional bowling alley. It is among the last remaining of a thriving mid-twentieth century culture of parish bowling alleys in the Archdiocese of St. Louis. Church recreation clubs and spaces have a long history in the US, dating at least as far back as the 19th-c. Bowling alleys like Epiphany Lanes in the 20th century seem to have been less motivated by the physical culture movement that produced the YMCA and other similar reform movements and more concerned with creating community spaces to bolster parish social ties and Catholic identities. 	8H86gZYSFIRHGy8q39OgBAfQFeC2	38.60640210352343	-90.30316317371744	\N	t	f	f	[]	2023-07-13 00:53:51.299	2023-07-13 00:53:51.299	2025-01-28 18:22:14.985	\N
