65bbdfa75d508d3d849520f9	Cathedral Basilica of Saint Louis	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706811734061.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Dome_Riley_002.JPG" width="436" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812133917.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Dome_Riley_001.JPG" width="433" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812171210.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Dome_Riley_003.JPG" width="434" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812204434.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Dome_Riley_004.JPG" width="432" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812235582.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Riley_001.JPG" width="432" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812271579.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190619_CathedralBasilica_Interior_Riley_002.JPG" width="430" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">When walking into the huge wooden doors of the Cathedral Basilica of St. Louis, it feels like stepping into another world. You are greeted with a giant and incredibly immaculate marble worship center. Many of the visitors, including myself, have let out an audible “wow” that feels natural upon entering the room. Among the hundreds of wooden pews in the room, huge groups of tourists walk around in awe of the beauty that surrounds them -- even in the middle of a weekday. As people enter the room, their eyes are immediately drawn to the intricate portraits on the ceiling and the shimmering gold tile that surrounds them. After that, the room draws their eyes to the main altar at the front, where Jesus hangs on the cross inside of an immaculate gazebo as a single spotlight shines on Him. Among the tour groups, families, couples, and individuals that enter the tall arches of the Cathedral, there is an unspoken rule of silence. Everyone understands that the sense of peace that the Church maintains would be broken with any loud noises. Compared to the gloomy sky and busy city streets that surround it, the Basilica offers the community a sense of peace and beauty simply upon stepping inside.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">How many people come here in a day? Are tour groups available every day?</span><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">How many people attend service here regularly?&nbsp;</span><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Is it the location or the legacy of the church that draws them in?</span></p><p></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Sounds of construction taking place at the back of the Church echo throughout the giant marble room eerily</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Tourists pour in and their soft footsteps noisily enter the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A tour group is wandering throughout the church, a man in a green shirt leading it. His voice fills the room as he describes each sculpture and ceiling painting in the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A young woman stands in front of the main altar, taking pictures on her camera. There are sounds from the lens focusing and then snapping the picture&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">As soon as people enter the room, the tend to gaze up towards the immaculate ceiling paintings</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Next, their eyes are drawn towards the altar at the front</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sounds of a drill in the back of the room disrupt the peaceful quiet of the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Everyone whispers, as if they don’t want to disrupt the atmosphere of the Church</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The ceilings are covered in paintings of religious figures, and behind the figures is gold tiles that make it look like the paintings are shining</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Every inch of the room is covered in immaculate artwork, even down to the wooden pews that have intricate engravings on every side</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">It seems as if every person is transported to a different place as they step inside the Cathedral. Their eyes fill with awe as soon as they look around</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A man tells his son “Wow. This is amazing.” as all of the altar lights are turned off except for one spotlight on a statue of Jesus</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">One mother holds her daughter in her lap in one of the pews and describes the artwork that is above them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">One family stands to the side of the cathedral, where there is a smaller altar with a portrait of Jesus. They silently light up the red candles in front of the portrait</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Everywhere you look, there is something new and elaborate that you notice. It feels as if you could stay in here forever and never see all of the intricate art</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A mom walks in with four daughters and the smallest among them shouts “WHOA!” as soon as she walks in the Church. The mother hurriedly tells her daughter that she must be quiet, as if not to disturb the sense of peace in the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">One woman sits three pews in front of me and bends down onto the kneeling bench to say her respects to the Jesus statue in front of us</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">One young couple sits a few pews behind me and sits silently next to each other, their eyes closed and heads back, seemingly praying</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The audience of the Cathedral is mostly families with children under 10, but there are many outliers to that in the crowd</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Some teen-aged boys walk into the main Church area and begin making odd noises that echo throughout the room, goofing around and calling each other stupid</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A mother makes her daughter stand in front of the main altar as she snaps pictures of her by the main Jesus statue</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The mother with four daughters whisper-yells at them as they aggressively pull down a kneeling bench that makes a loud thud as it drops to the floor</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The tour guide man in the green shirt talks at the back of the room, his voice echoes all the way to the front, but it is indistinguishable</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The Cathedral is one long room with two round areas jutting out from the sides, almost in the shape of a cross. There are entrances all around the front and back of the building, making it very accessible. Each of the circular side areas contain two confessional booths each, with deep green curtains in front of them. One side also has a marble holy water vat, while the other has the red candle vigil. The front altar has an immaculate gazebo-shaped structure, with different colored marble columns holding it up. There is a marble table at the front where the Priest speaks, a candle at each end of it and a table running spreading across it. Behind that is seven tall candles laid up against a marble structure that is used as a stage for the main sculpture. The entire focal point of the room stands on that marble structure in the gazebo, which is two disciples praising a giant crucified Jesus on an immaculate cross. Jesus has a halo surrounding his hanging head</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The Cathedral’s bell rings, signifying it is 2 o’clock</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The tour guide man speaks in between hammer noises from the construction, the hammer noises seem to completely affect the peaceful atmosphere</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The tour guide man stands directly next to my pew with his groups and begins to explain the artwork at the front of the room, the group is an older crowd that seem to ask questions after every piece of dialogue that the man says</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">He starts to explain all the different arches in the room and the religious figures displayed upon them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The room feels cold, although there is no movement of air in the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Celtic crosses with flor de lees inside are the engravings on each side of the pews</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are people buried in the crypt underneath the Church according to the tour guide</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The echoing of the tour guide’s voice in the room reminds me of religion because it sounds like a Priest’s voice echoing throughout the worship center as he gives a sermon</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">This room feels incredibly hard to explain, as it has so many intricate things inside of it, from the noises to the artwork to the people</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709242256501.mp4">Video 1</a></p><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709242269279.mp4">Video 2</a></p>	m5zMmy4slFNMTuX7a4kn6hIFumX2	38.64234975147799	-90.25491714477539	215 N Newstead Ave, St. Louis, MO 63108, USA	t	f	f	[{"label": "Catholicism", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "architecture", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "construction", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "art", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "awe", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "wonder", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "amazement", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "sound", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "acoustics", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "icons", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "signs", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "paintings", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "mosaic", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "beauty", "origin": "user"}]	2019-06-19 17:00:02.827	2024-02-01 18:15:03.191	2025-01-28 18:22:09.354	\N
