65e7aff2f53d3372e08459e5	Hobbit's Hole Antiques	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709682565845.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190617_HobbitsHoleAntiqueHouse_Exterior_Safa_001.JPG" width="617" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709682584456.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190617_HobbitsHoleAntiqueHouse_Exterior_Safa_003.JPG" width="620" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709682716191.mp4">Video 1</a></p><h4><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 11pt">The antique store popped out unlike other spots on Main Street. A large wooden sign, bags of mulch on a high mound of grass and dirt, an old green carriage with rose and the fuzzy sound of old tunes caught the attention of any passerby. Upon entering, I was met with clutter. Not the slightest bit unsightly, but all packed and tucked away into every nook and cranny of the small three-story house. The antiques were all old, though they weren’t all ancient. Some pieces such as Star Wars collectibles added a modern touch to what seemed to be an otherwise historic site. The creaky Maplewood flooring, the scent of mulch and stone, and the dust that covered most of these antiques made the place seem old, but a sudden change in the music added some life. 70s tunes turned into 21</span><sup><span style="font-size: 0.6em">st</span></sup><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 11pt"> century Bruno Mars’ jams after I heard a muffled male in the rooms at the back. Upon going closer, I noticed that it was just the radio playing. This spot clearly integrated the old with the new and showcased a passion for holding on the past and merging it with the present instead of failing to let go of old traditions.</span></h4><p></p><ol><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 11pt">Are people regular shoppers at this house and have they religiously sought out to maintain collections of their own?</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 11pt">What types of items sell the most?</span></p></li></ol>	h5IM6ZhPGxVEAdSpwywH4C1OZLB2	38.77374039577628	-90.48544496297832	1019 S Main St, St Charles, MO 63301, USA	f	f	f	[]	2019-06-17 17:00:12.395	2024-03-05 23:51:14.881	2024-06-21 21:25:18.885	\N
