69613774e5cae7d05d1f4f69	Cemetery	The cemetery is a place where religion, memory, and culture intersect visibly. The physical space is quiet and ordered, with headstones displaying religious symbols, language, and imagery. Some graves included crosses, Hebrew text, or Islamic inscriptions, showing how different traditions coexist within the same space. Connected to the story I brought for my Hospital field note, the cemetery is where I visited next. I observed visitors leaving flowers, standing silently, or speaking softly, engaging in rituals shaped by belief and culture.Being in this space made me feel reflective and aware of how religion shapes how people understand death and remembrance. The mood felt serious but not overwhelming. This site matters because it shows how religion influences how societies honor the dead and cope with loss. Cemeteries reflect lived religion through ritual, symbolism, and memory, demonstrating how beliefs continue to shape cultural practices even after life ends.	bgTpAnBRelfhaolDseUJ9wx1dqM2	-16.7363957	-49.1616131	7R7Q+C9 Goiânia, State of Goiás, Brazil	f	t	f	[]	2026-01-09 17:14:28.624	2026-01-09 17:14:28.72	2026-01-09 21:06:50.578	\N
6961a30de501b2dec4d9df5d	Mosque Note 1	<p>     The location of the Mosque I went to is off Weidman road and Manchester (<span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">519 Weidman Rd, Manchester, MO 63011), it functions much like a Catholic school within the Mosque. The building itself is large and has many additions as the community expanded, it has a beautiful copper dome with a tower outside making it look like one of the old traditional mosques. The inside has a main antechamber that then enters the main prayer room where first you have to first take your shoes off. Before Muslims pray they have a special cleaning routine called Wudu where they clean themselves, first they have to have intent to worship Allah, wash their hands, rinse mouth and nose, wash the face, arms, the head, and finally the feet. They do this three whole times before they pray to be presentably mentally and physically to Allah.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">      There were a mix of families as I arrived in the evening, this is one of the most active times for the mosque as people finish their day and come to pray. The building also has a school attached that acts as a k-12 option which acts similarly to a Catholic school. The building brings together more than just worshipers but a whole community. The people wore a mix of traditional Islamic dress and American styled clothing, there was a mixture of languages from people all over the middle east as well as English.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">     I enjoyed hearing about how many of the people came here as well as what Islam means to them, they are very traditional compared to some other religions in America however they are very kind and welcoming. There are people of all ethnicities there including black people, middle eastern people, and many white people. </span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">    The last time I had been to the Masjid was when I was a little kid with my grandpa, all I  remember is being in the prayer room and watching people talk in a foreign language, stand, and kneel in unison. It was very enlightening for me to be able to go again even though my beliefs do not align with Islam. I love the community and the people that are in it, they are incredibly kind and helpful. Many of my friends go to pray and have been encouraging me for awhile to go and I am so glad I went.</span></p><p></p><p></p>	uY69GLkeCrRFabQe3nkBlOvzpaj1	\N	\N	\N	f	t	f	[]	2026-01-10 00:53:23.426	2026-01-10 00:53:33.491	2026-01-10 10:36:13.151	\N
65c1340ef53d3372e0845922	The Jewel Box	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707160824360.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Pond_Riley_003.JPG" width="551" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707160895455.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Riley_001.JPG" width="549" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161007654.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Pond_Riley_001.JPG" width="552" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161061416.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Pond_Riley_002.JPG" width="550" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161112134.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Plants_Riley_003.JPG" width="548" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161153776.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Plants_Riley_002.JPG" width="548" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161209940.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_AliceMartinTurnSign_Riley.JPG" width="551" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161278009.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_LillyPoolsSign_Riley.JPG" width="546" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161350557.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Statue_Riley_002.JPG" width="539" style="aspect-ratio: 0.666667 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161481197.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_Statues_Riley_001.JPG" width="538" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161587565.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Exterior_SunDial_Riley.JPG" width="538" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161738225.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Interior_Plants_Riley_002.JPG" width="537" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161847778.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Interior_Riley_001.JPG" width="537" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707161906808.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Interior_Riley_003.JPG" width="535" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707162282357.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_Interior_Riley_004.JPG" width="536" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1707162335057.jpg" alt="LRDA_Location_20190712_TheJewelBox_TheJewelBoxSign_Riley.JPG" width="535" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Walking up to the grand entrance of the Jewel Box, I was completely enticed by the beauty of my surroundings. The cement sidewalk led to two koi ponds that have bright-colored water lilies floating on the top. Next to one of the ponds stands a statue of St. Francis of Assisi, who is known for his love of nature. He stands powerfully in front of some trees, with his arms raised above his dominion. I walked up the staircase that leads up to the glass doors, and pulled it open to a new world. Inside, a blast of cold air hit me as I looked up at all the plants almost reaching the high ceiling. I saw a huge wall of greenery as I paid my $1 admission fee to a security guard at the front. Beyond that, there was a large open space with a runway-looking area. A black carpet stretched across the floor with white chairs surrounding it, looking like the room was set up for a wedding. The plants were along the side walls and two shorter walls of plants were on either side of the room. Hanging planters were attached to the ceiling, connected by thick metal chains. The room was almost entirely green, except for a few spots of pink flowers that brightened the setting. The ceiling is all glass, so the bright blue sky with white puffy clouds were pouring through, looking like it was painted on. The only sounds that the visitors could hear were the air conditioner, the security guard’s phone quietly playing a video, and the occasional sound of a traffic driving by. If it weren’t for those occasional reminders that it is in the city, it would feel like a tropical paradise. Whether the visitors are there to plan their wedding or just to see some greenery, the Jewel Box is the perfect place for a quiet moment of reflection in a beautiful setting.</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">All of the visitors that I saw come into the Jewel Box were young couples. What were the visitors mostly there for, event planning or just for a visit?</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">What is the Jewel Box mostly known for?</span></p><p></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Does it drive many visitors to Forest Park, or do people come for other things and end up at the Jewel Box?</span></p><p></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The only sounds I can hear are the sound of the video playing on the security guard’s phone and the air conditioning blasting</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are some noises of trucks driving past in the distance</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">It’s freezing in here, which I didn’t expect – I thought it would need to stay humid for the plants</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The layout is also set up differently than I expected, it seems like it is set up for an event today</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There is a sort of runway in the middle of the floor with a long black rug, with potted plants along the sides of it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">It smells like a tropical destination in here and looks like it with tall palm trees on both sides of the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">An older couple walks in and pays the $1 admission fee, then slowly walks around the length of the building, looking at all the plants</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">They point to a few of them and talk about it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Once they arrive closer to the entrance, they take a seat in two of the twelve white chairs spread out across the room</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">They sit next to each other and stare up at the blue-sky peeking through the ceiling’s * The ceiling has four terraces that are layered along the edges of the glass, so that workers can get up there and maintain the spotlights</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There are many hanging planters that are held up by some of the terraces, they stand completely still on their metal chains</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">As another couple walks in to see the beauty, you can hear the processing of the security guard’s machine</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">They stand near the entrance and look all around them, they seem to be taken aback by the beauty as they walk into the main area</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Since the ceiling is all glass, the sky is completely visible through it. The blue-sky with white fluffy clouds almost looks painted on to the glass</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">All of the plants still have water droplets on them, showing that they just recently had their daily watering</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Outside, the trees that surround the building are swaying back and forth a bit in the breeze</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Nearby there are people using a leaf blower, a lawn mower, and a weed whacker, filling the air with those mechanical noises</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">It feels like a different location than the area that I entered, a much more tropical place</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The atmosphere is much calmer inside these walls than the city environment outside</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There is a balcony above the security guard’s stand that has two winding staircases on either side of it. Visitors can walk up them and see the view of the place in its entirety</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Since the woman in the couple that just walked in has a scooter for what looks like a broken foot, the man she is with climbs up it and explains what it looks like</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Since the air conditioning is on so high, some of the plants shake from the wind it’s creating</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The couple seems to be planning an event here, possibly a wedding, as they stand at the front and explain what they want to do with the space</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A new couple walks in, holding hands, looking at the beauty together</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Most of the plants in here seem tropical and have a palm-look to them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">While there is a lot of green, there are also some spots of pink in them, little pink flowers in the hanging planters, palms with a pink hue to them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">A loud airplane passes by overhead and is completely visible because of the large side windows</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The sound of a bus screeching to a halt comes closer and closer to the building, giving me a moment of realization that I’m still in the city, despite the peacefulness and quiet of the atmosphere</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">Outside, there stands a regal metal statue of a religious figure and an incredibly beautiful koi pond with bright lily pads floating in it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">The entrance to the Jewel Box is very grand and extravagant, there is a concrete path to the front door that walks by the statue and the koi pond, then exposes you to the giant glory of the glass building in front of you</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt">There doesn’t seem to be a crazy number of visitors in the middle of a random Thursday, but there is definitely more than I expected. So far, 100% of the visitors that I’ve seen have been Caucasian, middle to older aged heterosexual couples</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709328087102.mp4">Video 1</a></p><p></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1709328120502.mp4">Video 2</a></p>	m5zMmy4slFNMTuX7a4kn6hIFumX2	38.63515947497862	-90.28019428253174	JPP9+3W St. Louis, MO, USA	t	f	f	[{"label": "outdoors", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "architecture", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "art", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "statue", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "landscaping", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "plants", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "Catholicism", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "public", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "park", "origin": "user"}]	2019-07-12 17:00:22.041	2024-02-05 19:16:30.604	2025-01-28 18:22:11.887	\N
