66c74856986eb9dd86ee83fe	Catholic Figures Facing the Street in Williamsburg	<p>It's interesting that some of the windowsills in New York City have religious statues facing the street rather than, expectedly, inside the home. For some, it is done to protect the home from vandals and those who wish to harm. For some, it serves to remind the passers by of godliness. </p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1724336208692.jpg" alt="IMG_8951.jpeg" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1724336208693.jpg" alt="IMG_8952.jpeg" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	d2v7JCxLlFT9jkQlvayOD4Z3HAL2	40.7081156	-73.9570696	315 Broadway, Brooklyn, NY 11211, USA	f	f	f	[]	2024-08-22 14:14:04.729	2024-08-22 14:16:54.771	2026-04-15 13:48:37.076	\N
