674d23376c31e61d6ff373a5	Walk to Temple 16 (Kanonji)	<p>For walking henro, the journey between Temple 15 (Awa Kokubunji) and Temple 16 (Kanonji) requires walking along roads in a rural setting, along a highway, and through narrow extra urban streets. Along the route, various signs and waymarkers help to guide walking henro, as well as those traveling by car.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733108311367.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="437" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733108423571.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="435" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.065123009624685	134.47348237777098	Yano-385-4 Kokufuchō, Tokushima, 779-3126, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-12-02 02:52:12.465	2024-12-02 03:02:15.745	2026-04-15 13:48:39.184	\N
674d28362a34da641188e3c5	Temple 3 Hondo	<p>The main courtyard and hondo (main hall) at Temple 3 (Konsenji). This temple was fairly quiet, with only a few visitors and henro during our visit. As walking henro move away from Temple 1, the numbers tend to spread out. Henro and visitors traveling by car or tour bus also move through subsequent temples well before those who are walking between.</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733166503450.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="927" style="aspect-ratio: 1.3333333333333333">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.1473761	134.4685011	Konsenjihigashi-66 Kawabata, Itano, Itano District, Tokushima 779-0102, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-12-02 03:22:53.969	2024-12-02 03:23:34.047	2024-12-02 19:08:43.281	\N
674d29952a34da641188e3c6	Temple 4 Rules	<p>As the Shikoku Pilgrimage temples have welcomed an increasing number of visitors and <em>henro</em> (pilgrims) from around the world, including many who do not speak Japanese, some temples have made efforts to create multilingual signage and provide clear guidance on proper behavior and etiquette within the temple grounds.</p><p>This example from Temple 4 (<em>Dainichiji</em>) illustrates such efforts, featuring bilingual signage in Japanese and English. The sign not only helps visitors navigate the temple facilities, such as the dedicated parking area for pilgrims, but also outlines rules and etiquette to ensure respect for the sacred space. These initiatives make the pilgrimage more accessible and create a welcoming experience for international participants.</p><p></p><p>The content of the sign provides information about the No. 4 Dainichi-ji Temple ONLY Pilgrimage Parking Lot and outlines the following policies and guidelines:</p><p></p><ol><li><p>Private Management:<br>The temple property is privately managed, and visitors are required to follow the listed conditions.</p><p></p></li><li><p>Restricted Access:</p><ul><li><p>Only pilgrims are allowed to enter the property during the temple's official opening hours (8:00 AM to 5:00 PM).</p></li><li><p>The parking lot is exclusively for pilgrims.</p><p></p></li></ul></li><li><p>No Responsibility for Accidents:<br>The temple is not responsible for any accidents, damage, or injuries occurring on the property.</p><p></p></li><li><p>Prohibited Activities:</p><ul><li><p>Parking or driving vehicles other than for pilgrimage purposes.</p></li><li><p>Camping or overnight stays in the parking lot.</p></li><li><p>Smoking on temple premises.</p></li><li><p>Leaving garbage.</p></li><li><p>Entry of pets into the temple grounds.</p></li><li><p>Handling plants or flowers inappropriately.</p><p></p></li></ul></li><li><p>Stamp Office Hours:<br>The <em>nōkyō-sho</em> (stamp office) is open from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM daily.</p></li></ol><p>This sign demonstrates the temple’s efforts to maintain order, ensure safety, and promote respectful behavior among visitors and pilgrims,</p><p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1733110124531.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="925" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p></p><p></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0381842	134.4628974	Nishichō-263 Ichinomiyachō, Tokushima, 779-3132, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-12-02 03:26:04.592	2024-12-02 03:29:25.026	2024-12-03 20:42:07.473	\N
677301d71f40f09dc7c06d47	Statue of the Virgin Mary 	<p>This picture is of a statue of the Virgin Mary that my parents put on display all year round. My parents keep this statue on our mantle because it reminds them of their values and keeps them grounded in the Catholic faith. The Virgin Mary can symbolize many things, but my parents view her as the absolute perfection and gentleness that God and mary exude. By having her on the mantle, my parents can be reminded of the beauty and grace God has to offer. </p>	JKF57656uoXXZt6S4BtEqK0y6bv1	38.627798758648346	-90.336321198695	8373 Musick Memorial Dr, Brentwood, MO 63144, USA	f	f	f	[]	2024-12-30 20:25:58.965	2024-12-30 20:25:59.307	2024-12-30 20:35:06.274	\N
677ec21a9ab7f3dd8796687a	Bixby Avenue - Affton	<p>In this neighborhood, there were always many people on the street back then and we would always talk with one another and the younger ones would play together. There were a lot of trees lined up along the sidewalks, and a lot of greenery in general. A lot of holiday celebrations would be thrown as well, so there’d be neighborhood parties and a lot of cultural events. Fourth of July used to be a big thing here, and the whole neighborhood would gather to shoot fireworks and grill hot dogs. Religion played a part when it came to the holidays. Specifically, when it was Christmas, all the houses would be decorated and there’d be religious statues/figures all around the neighborhood. I would also always come to my best friend’s house to celebrate Christmas with her, even though I am not Christian myself.</p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736360464795.jpg"><p><br></p>	gb9lsunG6oXMjsxmLnXgzmYcXG82	38.55765518744356	-90.31074595186828	8527 Kathleen Ave, St. Louis, MO 63123, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-01-08 18:21:13.848	2025-01-08 18:21:14.081	2025-01-08 18:21:36.416	\N
678037299dcf3e02b0f6d803	Church of Scientology 	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736455960443.jpg" loading="lazy" width="4284" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75 / 1"><p><br>The Church of Scientology is a building that stands out every time you drive by with its elegant yet modern touch. Its grand stature and unique architecture make it a tough landmark to oversee. The S in the word scientology on the sign displays a resemblance of the classic Christian Cross but integrates its own twist with the triangles which is symbolic of its exclusive ideologies and belief system. Inside, the church is quiet and embodies a peaceful environment. According to a staff member, the church's goal is to express the intention of liberation from suffering and to aide individuals in accomplishing spiritual wisdom.</p>	rdhZC6H9O1bzb92yPQMyCM8WbPO2	38.66205925614059	-90.29577606558367	6124 Horton Pl, St. Louis, MO 63133, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-01-09 20:52:56.994	2025-01-09 20:52:57.155	2025-01-10 18:59:46.089	\N
678172e61132ef2b3c8f1d1a	Goodwill Religion	<p>The Goodwill on Manchester Road is a busy store that provides second-hand items for individuals in the Saint Louis community. Before entering the store, I noticed the strip mall the store was in. There were a variety of other businesses, including a sushi restaurant, a coding place, and a nail salon. The parking lot was quite full for a Thursday afternoon around 3 pm. When walking in, I was immediately greeted by a cashier who asked me how my day was and if I needed any help. After, I made my way through the store, taking in all of the items Goodwill was selling. Most were clothes, but they had a section for home goods as well. There were many different people in the store. Some were families with young children shopping for toys. Some were veterans who were viewing the clothes. And some were middle-aged women looking at the home goods. </p><p>Once I went back into the home section, I immediately came across a nativity scene in a large box. It was priced at $10.77. All of the pieces were inside and in great condition. The nativity scene was eight pieces total and included porcelain figures. The nativity scene most likely was from a Christian individual, who either did not need the nativity scene anymore or did not want it anymore. </p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736536751145.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><p>As I continued throughout the store, I noticed another home decor item, which was a small angel who was holding a cross. It had wings and was a woman with a long dress on that had gold detailing on the bottom. She was hugging the gold cross in her arms, holding it tightly. I did not check the price on this item, but if I had to guess, I would say it would be no more than $5. </p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736536772337.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="3024" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75"><p>After viewing the rest of the store, I was taking in the feeling of the store. It felt extremely comforting and homey. I am not sure if that is because the workers and fellow shoppers were extremely nice or if the second-hand items made that feeling. The lights were a soft white, and the store was playing quiet music on the speakers. When I left the store, the workers told me goodbye and wished me a happy new year. </p><p>Since this second-hand store was selling religious items, it makes me wonder why these items were there. Maybe the individual left their religion and went to another one, or maybe just left in general. Maybe the individual found another thing of the same item and liked it better. Maybe the individual was moving and did not need that item anymore. There are many possibilities as to why these items could be at the thrift store. This Goodwill shows how people incorporate their religion into most aspects of their life, whether that is in their clothing, house decor, or jewelry. I believe that this store allowed me to see the possibilities as to why some people are getting rid of these religious items and what that means in our society. Are more people leaving their churches or shopping more often? We may never find the answer; however, looking at the items and analyzing the meaning of them helps our society grow in our knowledge about this topic. </p><p></p>	eNlFMkamG3dhAy0n4WcBAcZECOm2	38.59427120000001	-90.5140412	14373 Manchester Rd, Manchester, MO 63011, USA	f	f	f	[{"label": "goodwill", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "second-hand", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "thrift", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "religion", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "Christian", "origin": "user"}]	2025-01-09 19:03:46.309	2025-01-10 19:20:06.462	2025-01-11 03:08:28.207	\N
6781f4e19ab7f3dd87966887	Boston Aquarium 	<p>The Boston Aquarium is a modern building with a path to follow through all the exhibits. This allowed me to experience all different kinds of animals which I would never have been able to see. I shared this experience with those around me. There were many families with little kids running around excited by all the animals. Seeing the kids run around excited showed me that this was more than a place to see cool animals. This was a place where many become intrigued by the world around them. The kids would press their faces against the glass to get a closer look at the fish. The aquarium was a safe place for this kids, from all over the city, to come and explore the world of fish. There were kids talking with each other and pointing out different fish. After reflecting upon my time at the Boston Aquarium I have a deeper appreciation for place where people can explore the world together. This ties into religion as none of the kids were concerned about another religion, they were all intrigued by the fish and exploring what the world had to offer.</p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736570070666.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736570075622.jpg"><p><br></p><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736570078976.jpg"><p><br></p>	b4GD3PejFOXBgLEzgOBazwi5uyg2	38.95743188766581	-77.0758211997844	3808 Huntington St NW, Washington, DC 20015, USA	t	f	f	[]	2025-01-11 04:34:41.173	2025-01-11 04:34:41.621	2025-01-11 04:34:51.03	\N
678484ba9dcf3e02b0f6d80d	Modern Cross?	<p>On Gravois, right before highway 44 there's a lopsided cross. There's nothing detailing why it's there or if the uneven nature of it indicates anything. Modern cross or abstract art and a statement? </p>	GHHBmf2Y5RQTXN1drNatuiZUqf63	38.60739977893956	-90.21491409176025	2114 Lemp Ave, St. Louis, MO 63104, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-01-13 03:04:57.635	2025-01-13 03:12:58.001	2026-04-15 13:48:39.743	\N
6782e72f1132ef2b3c8f1d1e	Mississippi Palisades State Park	<p></p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736632773437.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="675" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1736632793045.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="678" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5 / 1"><p>Located among the Mississippi River in northwestern Illinois, the Palisades State Park stands as an example of God in nature. Many religions believe that the world around us is proof that there is a God, these pictures show that. The area is quiet, fairly devoid of outside noise outside of the passing of cars on the remote highway far below the lookout point. While there you may encounter one of the many freight trains transporting items along the river. The park is also home to a great deal of wildlife that is hard to find anywhere else.</p>	vkXhcfUpNogQCZia3cvpO8pJ44G3	42.127042228707026	-90.15658436878662	13834 IL-84, Savanna, IL 61074, USA	f	f	f	[]	2025-01-11 21:48:31.099	2025-01-11 21:48:31.569	2025-01-11 22:07:52.892	\N
