6627f904a1162cbdb9d34a59	Stone towers at Bulguksa Temple	<img src="TypeError: Network request failed" style="\n      max-width: 50%;\n      height: auto; /* Maintain aspect ratio */\n      /* Additional CSS properties for sizing */\n    ">&nbsp;<br><img src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1713895279265.jpg" style="\n      max-width: 50%;\n      height: auto; /* Maintain aspect ratio */\n      /* Additional CSS properties for sizing */\n    ">&nbsp;<br><div><br></div><div>I saw these little stone towers on the grounds of the Bulguksa Temple complex in Gyeongju, South Korea during an internship experience I had. These towers were constructed by practitioners of Mahayana Buddhism, common to Korea as a region. They are said to represent stability and balance, concepts that are heavily emphasized in this strain of Korean Buddhism.</div>	wQuX42m58oM65OP2GTRSmsNiP6B2	38.64691843123039	-90.30639219223914	247 Orange St, University City, MO 63130, USA	f	f	f	[]	2023-07-12 19:07:00	2024-04-23 18:08:04.216	2024-06-21 20:54:46.574	\N
