6646fb8f3a48ef5557d2b71b	Waymarker - Journey to Temple 4	<p>One small, but important detail about the journey between temples for the walking henro are the way markers that are placed along the route most commonly used. These markers come in a variety of forms, with older wooden and stone markers mixed with laminated paper sheets and even painted markers on the ground or a nearby object (such as a guardrail).</p><p></p><p>With modern access to smartphone navigation, we observed many henro using their phones, but as our team traced the route between Temple 3 and Temple 4 on foot ourselves we found we often needed the way markers we encountered to verify we were on the path to the next temple.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1715927852005.jpg" alt="20240514_105713.jpg" loading="lazy" width="3000" style="aspect-ratio: 0.75">	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	34.0765913	134.5590113	Japan, 〒770-0815 Tokushima, Suketōbashi, 1-chōme−２２ 鈴木商店渭水ビル	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-17 06:36:12.433	2024-05-17 06:39:11.544	2024-06-21 20:55:24.324	\N
664c0f608aad2c5255e531e4	Temple 23 	<p>Temple 23, Yakuoji, is located on a hillside in Minami in Tokushima Prefecture. This the last temple in Tokushima prefecture, and the last in what is considered the first dojo, before a long distance to Temple 24 in Kochi Prefecture.</p><img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1732672082031.jpg" alt="Image description" loading="lazy" width="866" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p></p><p>Due to its location on a hillside overlooking the sea and the seaside village of Hiwasa, Yakuoji is tiered with multiple levels. The Hondo and Daishido on 3rd level, while the temple's Pagoda is above this terrace. Near street level is the temple's stamp office and shop. With visitors also coming to the area for its other attractions, the atmosphere at this temple is a bit more relaxed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>	KHAHfSWMJ6SshJHmk81TXGOPUzI3	33.7322219	134.5289377	Teramae-233-4 Okugawachi, Minami, Kaifu District, Tokushima 779-2305, Japan	f	f	f	[]	2024-05-21 03:03:42.587	2024-05-21 03:05:04.071	2024-12-02 02:05:23.59	\N
