69616d18e501b2dec4d9df5b	Holy Trinity Cathedral (Sameba)	<p>The Holy Trinity Cathedral (aka Sameba) dominates the horizon of Tbilisi in a way that you can never ignore it. If you put yourself on a slightly elevated position anywhere in Tbilisi, you WILL see the Holy Trinity Cathedral. As you approach it the space feels both religious and civic at the same time. People move between casual conversations and prayers, which emphasizes the fact that this cathedral functions not only as a site of worship but also as a public landmark.</p><p></p><p>Inside, the vastness of the interior create a sense of humility. Candles and icons appear all around you. Worshippers cross themselves, kiss icons, stand quietly in a prayer, etc.</p><p></p><p>What's truly impressive is how Georgian Orthodox identity feels inseparable from national identity in this space. Sameba does not feel like a church removed from public life. It anchors religion and belonging in modern Georgia.</p>	MnFDBFJqBrbcnAHKMcrBSGGu6HS2	41.69757197322683	44.81682926416397	MRX8+3H8, Gumbri II Dead End, T'bilisi, Georgia	t	f	f	[]	2026-01-05 21:03:12.96	2026-01-09 21:03:20.905	2026-01-13 23:47:58.466	\N
