65bbe3b4f53d3372e084591e	Mary Bruemmer Room (SLU)	<img height="auto" src="https://livedreligion.s3.amazonaws.com/media-1706812290429.jpg" width="4032" style="aspect-ratio: 1.33333 / 1"><p>&nbsp;<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Demonstrating the Where's Religion? apps to the&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 1em">ad hoc campus advisory committee for the brand new Center on Lived Religion!&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em">The Mary Bruemmer conference room is in DuBourg Hall on the campus of Saint Louis University. Bishop Louis William Valentine DuBourg was a French Catholic who emigrated to the United States after the French Revolution and was instrumental in the founding of what would become Saint Louis University. He was a documented enslaver and also spearheaded several Catholic boarding schools among local indigenous peoples. Both enslavement and settler colonialism are part of DuBourg's legacy. The Center on Lived Religion thus also benefits from these histories of enslavement and displacement.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em">Mary Bruemmer was a SLU alumna (Class of 1942) who returned in 1956 to work as an administrator and volunteer until her death in 2021 at the age of 101. Among other efforts, she served as Dean of Women, Dean of Students, and founded the Women's Commission.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em">We acknowledge both of these legacies in the life and work of SLU and in the Center on Lived Religion.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.pbs.org/newshour/amp/education/uncovering-the-traumatic-history-of-one-native-american-boarding-school-in-the-midwest">https://www.pbs.org/newshour/amp/education/uncovering-the-traumatic-history-of-one-native-american-boarding-school-in-the-midwest</a><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.slu.edu/news/2021/december/mary-bruemmer-obituary.php">https://www.slu.edu/news/2021/december/mary-bruemmer-obituary.php</a><span style="font-size: 1em"><br></span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>	8H86gZYSFIRHGy8q39OgBAfQFeC2	38.636121898960596	-90.23347348731785	DuBourg Hall, 221 N Grand Blvd, St. Louis, MO 63103, USA	f	f	f	[{"label": "COLR meeting", "origin": "user"}, {"label": "SLU", "origin": "user"}]	2024-02-01 18:30:56.319	2024-02-01 18:32:20.483	2025-01-28 18:22:09.101	\N
